```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Circular Radius Slider</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .slider-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 300px; /* Desired canvas width */
            height: 300px; /* Desired canvas height */
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            cursor: grab;
            touch-action: none; /* Prevents scrolling on touch devices */
        }
        .slider-container:active {
            cursor: grabbing;
        }
        #radiusCanvas {
            display: block;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            background-color: #fff;
        }
        .value-display {
            font-size: 1.5em;
            margin-top: 10px;
            padding: 5px 10px;
            background-color: #fff;
            border-radius: 5px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="slider-container">
        <canvas id="radiusCanvas"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="value-display">Selected Radius: <span id="currentValue">50</span></div>

    <script>
        class CircularRadiusSlider {
            constructor(canvasId, options = {}) {
                this.canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);
                if (!this.canvas) {
                    console.error("Canvas element not found!");
                    return;
                }
                this.ctx = this.canvas.getContext('2d');

                // Default options
                this.config = {
                    minValue: 0,
                    maxValue: 100,
                    initialValue: 50,
                    minRadius: 20,       // Smallest visual radius
                    maxRadius: Math.min(this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height) / 2 - 10, // Largest visual radius, with padding
                    numMarkers: 5,       // Number of concentric marker circles (e.g., 0%, 25%, 50%, 75%, 100%)
                    step: 1,             // Snap to steps of this size
                    centerMarkColor: '#333',
                    markerColor: '#ddd',
                    activeCircleColor: 'rgba(0, 123, 255, 0.7)',
                    activeCircleBorderColor: 'rgba(0, 80, 180, 1)',
                    onValueChanged: (value) => {
                        document.getElementById('currentValue').textContent = Math.round(value);
                    },
                    ...options
                };

                // Ensure maxRadius is not smaller than minRadius
                if (this.config.maxRadius <= this.config.minRadius) {
                    this.config.maxRadius = this.config.minRadius + 50; // Ensure some range
                    console.warn("maxRadius was too small, adjusted to:", this.config.maxRadius);
                }


                this.canvas.width = this.canvas.parentElement.clientWidth;
                this.canvas.height = this.canvas.parentElement.clientHeight;

                // Recalculate maxRadius based on actual canvas dimensions
                this.config.maxRadius = Math.min(this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height) / 2 - 10;
                 if (this.config.maxRadius <= this.config.minRadius) {
                    this.config.maxRadius = this.config.minRadius + Math.min(this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height) / 4;
                    console.warn("maxRadius was still too small after resize, adjusted to:", this.config.maxRadius);
                }


                this.centerX = this.canvas.width / 2;
                this.centerY = this.canvas.height / 2;

                this.currentValue = this.config.initialValue;
                this.currentRadius = this._valueToRadius(this.currentValue);
                this.isDragging = false;

                this._setupEventListeners();
                this.render();
                if (this.config.onValueChanged) {
                    this.config.onValueChanged(this.currentValue);
                }
            }

            _setupEventListeners() {
                this.canvas.addEventListener('mousedown', this._handleStart.bind(this));
                this.canvas.addEventListener('touchstart', this._handleStart.bind(this), { passive: false });

                window.addEventListener('mousemove', this._handleMove.bind(this));
                window.addEventListener('touchmove', this._handleMove.bind(this), { passive: false });

                window.addEventListener('mouseup', this._handleEnd.bind(this));
                window.addEventListener('touchend', this._handleEnd.bind(this));

                // Optional: Recalculate on resize
                window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
                    this.canvas.width = this.canvas.parentElement.clientWidth;
                    this.canvas.height = this.canvas.parentElement.clientHeight;
                    this.centerX = this.canvas.width / 2;
                    this.centerY = this.canvas.height / 2;
                    this.config.maxRadius = Math.min(this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height) / 2 - 10;
                     if (this.config.maxRadius <= this.config.minRadius) {
                        this.config.maxRadius = this.config.minRadius + Math.min(this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height) / 4;
                     }
                    this.currentRadius = this._valueToRadius(this.currentValue); // Recalculate current radius
                    this.render();
                });
            }

            _getMousePos(event) {
                const rect = this.canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
                let clientX, clientY;
                if (event.touches && event.touches.length > 0) {
                    clientX = event.touches[0].clientX;
                    clientY = event.touches[0].clientY;
                } else {
                    clientX = event.clientX;
                    clientY = event.clientY;
                }
                return {
                    x: clientX - rect.left,
                    y: clientY - rect.top
                };
            }

            _handleStart(event) {
                event.preventDefault(); // Prevent text selection or other default browser actions
                this.isDragging = true;
                this.canvas.style.cursor = 'grabbing';
                this._updateFromEvent(event);
            }

            _handleMove(event) {
                if (!this.isDragging) return;
                event.preventDefault();
                this._updateFromEvent(event);
            }

            _handleEnd() {
                if (!this.isDragging) return;
                this.isDragging = false;
                this.canvas.style.cursor = 'grab';
            }

            _updateFromEvent(event) {
                const pos = this._getMousePos(event);
                const dx = pos.x - this.centerX;
                const dy = pos.y - this.centerY;
                let newRadius = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);

                // Clamp radius
                newRadius = Math.max(this.config.minRadius, Math.min(newRadius, this.config.maxRadius));

                this.currentRadius = newRadius;
                let newValue = this._radiusToValue(this.currentRadius);

                // Snap to step
                if (this.config.step > 0) {
                    newValue = Math.round(newValue / this.config.step) * this.config.step;
                    // Ensure value is within min/max after snapping
                    newValue = Math.max(this.config.minValue, Math.min(newValue, this.config.maxValue));
                    this.currentRadius = this._valueToRadius(newValue); // Update radius based on snapped value
                }

                this.currentValue = newValue;

                this.render();
                if (this.config.onValueChanged) {
                    this.config.onValueChanged(this.currentValue);
                }
            }

            _radiusToValue(radius) {
                if (this.config.maxRadius === this.config.minRadius) return this.config.minValue; // Avoid division by zero
                const percentage = (radius - this.config.minRadius) / (this.config.maxRadius - this.config.minRadius);
                let value = this.config.minValue + percentage * (this.config.maxValue - this.config.minValue);
                return Math.max(this.config.minValue, Math.min(value, this.config.maxValue));
            }

            _valueToRadius(value) {
                if (this.config.maxValue === this.config.minValue) return this.config.minRadius; // Avoid division by zero
                const percentage = (value - this.config.minValue) / (this.config.maxValue - this.config.minValue);
                let radius = this.config.minRadius + percentage * (this.config.maxRadius - this.config.minRadius);
                return Math.max(this.config.minRadius, Math.min(radius, this.config.maxRadius));
            }

            setValue(newValue) {
                newValue = Math.max(this.config.minValue, Math.min(newValue, this.config.maxValue));
                 // Snap to step if setting programmatically
                if (this.config.step > 0) {
                    newValue = Math.round(newValue / this.config.step) * this.config.step;
                    newValue = Math.max(this.config.minValue, Math.min(newValue, this.config.maxValue));
                }
                this.currentValue = newValue;
                this.currentRadius = this._valueToRadius(this.currentValue);
                this.render();
                if (this.config.onValueChanged) {
                    this.config.onValueChanged(this.currentValue);
                }
            }

            getValue() {
                return this.currentValue;
            }

            render() {
                this.ctx.clearRect(0, 0, this.canvas.width, this.canvas.height);

                // Draw Markers
                if (this.config.numMarkers > 1) {
                    this.ctx.strokeStyle = this.config.markerColor;
                    this.ctx.lineWidth = 1;
                    for (let i = 0; i < this.config.numMarkers; i++) {
                        const fraction = i / (this.config.numMarkers - 1);
                        const markerRadius = this.config.minRadius + fraction * (this.config.maxRadius - this.config.minRadius);
                        if (markerRadius > 0) { // Only draw if radius is positive
                             this.ctx.beginPath();
                             this.ctx.arc(this.centerX, this.centerY, markerRadius, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
                             this.ctx.stroke();
                        }
                    }
                }

                // Draw Active Circle
                if (this.currentRadius > 0) {
                    this.ctx.beginPath();
                    this.ctx.arc(this.centerX, this.centerY, this.currentRadius, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
                    this.ctx.fillStyle = this.config.activeCircleColor;
                    this.ctx.fill();
                    this.ctx.strokeStyle = this.config.activeCircleBorderColor;
                    this.ctx.lineWidth = 2;
                    this.ctx.stroke();
                }


                // Draw Center Mark
                this.ctx.beginPath();
                this.ctx.arc(this.centerX, this.centerY, 3, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
                this.ctx.fillStyle = this.config.centerMarkColor;
                this.ctx.fill();
            }
        }

        // --- Initialize the slider ---
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            const slider = new CircularRadiusSlider('radiusCanvas', {
                minValue: 0,
                maxValue: 200,
                initialValue: 75,
                minRadius: 15,      // Smallest selectable radius
                // maxRadius will be calculated based on canvas size
                numMarkers: 6,      // e.g., 0, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100% of range
                step: 5,            // Snap to steps of 5
                activeCircleColor: 'rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.6)',
                activeCircleBorderColor: 'rgba(200, 50, 50, 1)',
                markerColor: '#cccccc',
                onValueChanged: (value) => {
                    document.getElementById('currentValue').textContent = value.toFixed(0); // Format if needed
                    console.log("Slider value:", value);
                }
            });

            // Example of setting value programmatically
            // setTimeout(() => {
            //     slider.setValue(150);
            // }, 2000);
        });

    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Key Improvements and Explanations:**

1.  **Class-based Structure:** `CircularRadiusSlider` makes it reusable and organized.
2.  **Configuration Object:** Pass options like `minValue`, `maxValue`, `colors`, etc., during instantiation.
3.  **Dynamic Sizing:**
    *   The canvas dimensions are set to match its parent container (`slider-container`).
    *   `maxRadius` is calculated based on the actual canvas size, ensuring it fits.
    *   A `resize` event listener is added to update dimensions and re-render if the window size changes.
4.  **Touch Support:** `touchstart`, `touchmove`, `touchend` are handled alongside mouse events. `event.preventDefault()` is used in touch handlers to prevent page scroll during drag. `passive: false` is important for this. `touch-action: none;` on the container helps.
5.  **Event Listener Scope:** Mouse/touch move and end listeners are attached to `window` so dragging can continue even if the cursor leaves the canvas, and then correctly stops.
6.  **`_getMousePos` Helper:** Correctly calculates mouse/touch position relative to the canvas.
7.  **Value Clamping & Mapping:**
    *   `_radiusToValue` and `_valueToRadius` handle the conversion.
    *   Values and radii are clamped to their respective min/max.
8.  **Snapping to Steps:**
    *   The `step` option allows the value to snap. The radius is then recalculated from the snapped value to ensure visual consistency.
9.  **`onValueChanged` Callback:** Allows you to react to value changes outside the slider class.
10. **Clear Drawing:** `ctx.clearRect()` is used before each `render()`.
11. **Defensive Checks:** Added checks for `maxRadius` vs `minRadius` to prevent issues.
12. **Accessibility Hint:** `cursor: grab` and `cursor: grabbing` provide visual feedback for draggable state. For true accessibility, ARIA roles (`role="slider"`, `aria-valuenow`, etc.) would be needed, but that's more complex with canvas.
13. **`passive: false` for Touch Events:** This is important when you want to call `event.preventDefault()` within a touch event listener to prevent default browser actions like scrolling.
14. **Initial Value Display:** The `onValueChanged` callback is now called after initialization to set the initial display.
15. **`setValue` Method:** Allows programmatic control of the slider's value.

This provides a robust and customizable circular radius slider. You can adjust the `options` in the `new CircularRadiusSlider(...)` call to change its behavior and appearance.

