    *   Added a check for `deletePhotoModalElement` before trying to add an event listener to it, to prevent errors if it doesn't exist on the page.
    *   Added a small section in `show.bs.modal` to clear any previous custom validation states, though native HTML5 validation usually handles this well on its own.

Now, when you click the "Save Changes" button:
1.  The browser will first check if `title` has at least 1 character and not more than 100.
2.  It will check if `desc` has not more than 5000 characters.
3.  If any of these fail, the browser will show a validation message (e.g., "Please fill out this field." or "Please lengthen this text to 1 character or more.") and the form submission will be blocked.
4.  If all validations pass, the `submit` event on the form will fire, `event.preventDefault()` will be called, and then your `fn.popupActionHandler.submit('editFormPhoto')` will execute.

